    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0647" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg633"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing, Attorney-General, to Mr. McKeon, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney-General’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1856-01-19"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 19, 1856</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 16th instant, in relation to the retention of the
                    revenue-cutter Washington at the port of New York, and have submitted the same
                    to the Secretary of the Treasury. I am informed by him that he has countermanded
                    the orders requiring the Washington to leave New York on a cruise, and directed
                    her to remain there.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>C. CUSHING.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">John McKeon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">United States District Attorney.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
